.TH sleep "" "Command"
.SH NAME
sleep \- suspend execution for a specified time
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsleep \fIseconds\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
sleep -- suspend execution for a specified time
Usage:	sleep seconds
.HE
.B sleep
suspends execution of the current process for
.I seconds
seconds, then exits.
.I seconds
must be given as a string of decimal digits.
.PP
.B sleep
is most often used inside shell scripts, to pace a sequence of commands
or to poll for some condition at intervals.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B sleep
complains and exits if it is given more than one argument, or if
.I seconds
contains anything other than decimal digits.
